I totally agree with you. Nethack already has more voluntary challenges 
than anyone can play. How many people ascended every class in a 
"stylish" way (nude caveman, illiterate barbarian, ...)? I for sure 
didn't...

IMHO trying to make the late-game more challenging by adding nasty stuff 
to Gehennom mainly adds boredom by slowing everything down, and it 
removes creative solutions. (the last 40 levels of Angband are just awful)

The Lethe-patch once was a nice try. For someone who likes power-gaming 
and extionctionists Slash'EM with the Lethe-patch would be surely nice, 
but I think it's still a lot less challenging than vanilla Nethack can be.

